    "ff_count": 67007,
    "clock_mhz": 25.0,
    "fpga_clock_mhz": 121.0,
    "offchip_kb": 64,
    "stated_util": 0.46,
    "blocks_mm2": {
     "cores": 23.79,
     "npus": 17.73,
     "operand_banks": 2.7,
     "glue": 2.0
    }
   },
   "notes": "The measured design is pad-limited at 28 nm, not transistor-limited: 1.35M gates is under a square millimetre on GRX28. Density levers buy power and integration headroom here, not a smaller die. 7.5T is the default because the 9T baseline saves only a fraction of a pad-ring die. The pin budget, not the cell library, is the largest remaining area lever: deleting the 64-bit bus frees more die than every DTCO step combined."
  },
